^SAMPLE = GSM2588688
!Sample_title = TE 2_RNA-seq
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM2588688
!Sample_status = Public on Apr 13 2018
!Sample_submission_date = Apr 25 2017
!Sample_last_update_date = May 15 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Mouse embryo
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: trophoblast
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = strain: B6D2F1 (C57BL/6 x DB/2)
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = For gene knockdown，small interference RNAs (siRNAs) against mouse Chaf1a, Sumo2, Setdb1, Ube2i and Zfp809 were diluted in nuclease-free water to 20 μM. The siRNAs for a given gene were mixed for knock-down, with a working concentration of 5 μM. Oocytes were injected with approximately 10 pL of siRNAs using a Piezo-driven micromanipulator. Allow oocytes to recover for at least 1 h in the incubator prior to Intracytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI). The sperm head was then injected into the oocyte according to the method described previously (Kimura and Yanagimachi, 1995). The injected embryos were observed and summarized from the 2-cell stage to blastocyst stage.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For MII oocyte and cleavage-stage embryos, the zona pellucida of embryos was removed by 0.5% pronase E (Sigma). Then the embryo was incubated in Ca2+ free CZB for 5 min. Polar bodies were removed by gentle pipetting using an inner diameter of 120 μm fire polished glass needle. For ICM and TE isolation, the zona pellucida of blastocysts was removed by 0.5% pronase E (Sigma). They were then incubated for 20 min in Ca2+ free CZB，the tight junctions TE cells and ICM cells were separated by gently pipetting in a pipette with a diameter of 40-60 μm.For epiblast (Epi) and extraembryonic ectoderm (Exe) isolation, embryos were cuttted at the embryonic/extraembryonic boundary using properly sharpened forceps. A fire-polished glass needle whose inner diameter is silghtly smaller than the width of the embryonic/extraembryonic fragment was used for separating epiblast or extraembryonic ectoderm from the visceral endoderm, and the epiblast or extraembryonic ectoderm were then incubated in Ca2+-free CZB for 10 min. Single cells were separated by gentle pipetting using a fire-polished glass needle with an inner diameter of 15-20 μm.200 cells were washed three times in 0.5% BSA-PBS solution per reaction.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were prepared according to Ovation® RNA‑Seq System V2 (NuGEN, 7102) following the manufacturer’s instructions.
!Sample_data_processing = Illumina Casava1.8 software used for basecalling.
!Sample_data_processing = Sequenced reads were trimmed for adaptor sequence, low quality and low complexity reads, then mapped to mm9 reference genome using tophat v1.3.3 with default parameters.
!Sample_data_processing = Gene expression for each sample was quantified to RPKM using Cufflinks(v 1.2.0).
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm9
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Tab-delimited text files include RPKM values for each transcript.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL13112
!Sample_contact_name = Shaorong,,Gao
!Sample_contact_laboratory = Gaolab
!Sample_contact_department = School of life science and technology
